"<div class="page cr-page" style="max-width:900px"><div class="cr-top"><div class="score cr-ring bad" style="--deg:136.8deg">38<small>/100</small></div><div><h1 style="margin:0">Code review</h1><div class="sub notr" style="margin:0">svc/load.rs</div></div><span style="flex:1"></span><button class="mini">Open file</button></div>
   <div class="sub" style="margin-top:12px">Rule-based checks for correctness, security, performance and the project rules. They point at evidence; you decide what to change.</div><div class="cr-chips"><button class="cr-chip on">All <b>3</b></button><button class="cr-chip sev-bug"><i></i>bug <b>2</b></button><button class="cr-chip sev-risk"><i></i>risk <b>1</b></button><button class="cr-chip sev-perf" disabled=""><i></i>perf <b>0</b></button><button class="cr-chip sev-style" disabled=""><i></i>style <b>0</b></button></div><div class="crf-list"><div class="crf sev-bug">
    <div class="crf-h"><span class="tag sev-bug">bug</span><b>Loop iterates over a clone of the iterator</b><span class="sp"></span><span class="lnk">L3</span></div>
    <div class="cr-code notr"><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">1</span><span class="tx"><span class="kw">fn</span> <span class="fn">load</span>(conn: &amp;<span class="ty">Connection</span>) -&gt; <span class="ty">Vec</span>&lt;<span class="ty">Row</span>&gt; {</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">2</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">let</span> v = <span class="fn">parse</span>().<span class="fn">unwrap</span>();</span></div><div class="cr-cl mark"><span class="ln">3</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">for</span> c <span class="kw">in</span> it.<span class="fn">clone</span>() { <span class="fn">use_it</span>(c); }</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">4</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">let</span> sql = <span class="str">"SELECT id FROM t WHERE ws = ?1 LIMIT ?2"</span>;</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">5</span><span class="tx">    v</span></div></div><div class="crf-b"><p>The original iterator never advances, so any check after the loop (like <code>peek()</code>) sees stale state.</p><p><b>Suggested:</b> Use <code>.by_ref()</code> to keep one cursor.</p></div>
    <div class="crf-acts"><button class="btn ghost">Go to line</button><span class="sp"></span><button class="btn ghost">Dismiss</button></div>
  </div><div class="crf sev-bug">
    <div class="crf-h"><span class="tag sev-bug">bug</span><b>LIMIT without ORDER BY</b><span class="sp"></span><span class="lnk">L4</span></div>
    <div class="cr-code notr"><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">2</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">let</span> v = <span class="fn">parse</span>().<span class="fn">unwrap</span>();</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">3</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">for</span> c <span class="kw">in</span> it.<span class="fn">clone</span>() { <span class="fn">use_it</span>(c); }</span></div><div class="cr-cl mark"><span class="ln">4</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">let</span> sql = <span class="str">"SELECT id FROM t WHERE ws = ?1 LIMIT ?2"</span>;</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">5</span><span class="tx">    v</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">6</span><span class="tx">}</span></div></div><div class="crf-b"><p>SQLite returns rows in whatever order is cheapest; “recent” lists become arbitrary.</p><p><b>Suggested:</b> Add <code>ORDER BY created_at DESC</code> and an index on (filter, order) columns.</p></div>
    <div class="crf-acts"><button class="btn ghost">Go to line</button><span class="sp"></span><button class="btn ghost">Dismiss</button></div>
  </div><div class="crf sev-risk">
    <div class="crf-h"><span class="tag sev-risk">risk</span><b>unwrap() on a fallible value</b><span class="sp"></span><span class="lnk">L2</span></div>
    <div class="cr-code notr"><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">1</span><span class="tx"><span class="kw">fn</span> <span class="fn">load</span>(conn: &amp;<span class="ty">Connection</span>) -&gt; <span class="ty">Vec</span>&lt;<span class="ty">Row</span>&gt; {</span></div><div class="cr-cl mark"><span class="ln">2</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">let</span> v = <span class="fn">parse</span>().<span class="fn">unwrap</span>();</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">3</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">for</span> c <span class="kw">in</span> it.<span class="fn">clone</span>() { <span class="fn">use_it</span>(c); }</span></div><div class="cr-cl"><span class="ln">4</span><span class="tx">    <span class="kw">let</span> sql = <span class="str">"SELECT id FROM t WHERE ws = ?1 LIMIT ?2"</span>;</span></div></div><div class="crf-b"><p>Panics on bad input and takes the whole service down.</p><p><b>Suggested:</b> Return a typed error with <code>?</code> or map it.</p></div>
    <div class="crf-acts"><button class="btn ghost">Go to line</button><span class="sp"></span><button class="btn ghost">Dismiss</button></div>
  </div></div></div>"
`;

